{
  "id": 438223778,
  "iid": 22616,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "epan: Use unsigned offsets in tvb_ensure_*_length_remaining",
  "description": "tvb_ensure_captured_length_remaining and\ntvb_ensure_reported_length_remaining are not called with negative offsets\nintended to mean \"offset before the end of the (captured) length\" in any\nchecked in code in the repository and never have been. It doesn't seem\nuseful to do that, particularly not for the reported length. Negative\noffsets, where supported, are always counted from the end of the *captured*\ndata, which is not particularly well-documented and likely to be unexpected\nwhen using a routine that measures the reported length and a tvbuff with\ncaptured length less than the reported length.\n\nJust require the offsets to be unsigned. This means that if a signed\ninteger representing an offset has overflowed, it will be treated as\na really big integer and almost surely throw an exception. That is\nthe desired behavior when calling these functions.\n\nAlso, document the different behavior of the two functions where the\noffset is just past the end of the data. Presumably for historical\nreasons, tvb_ensure_captured_length_remaining never returns 0, always\nrequiring at least 1 octet of data remaining, but by contrast\ntvb_ensure_reported_length_remaining will return 0 for an offset just\npast the end of the data.\n\nPing #20103",
  "state": "merged",
